Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat: translate enhancement catalog (Boutique Stays,
 Private Transfer, ...)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

enhancement_content (title/description/button texts) had zero
translation wiring — confirmed on a live proposal, all three
enhancements always rendered in English regardless of locale.

- New migration: enhancement_content_translations table, same
  shape/RLS policy as experience_content_translations.
- translateEnhancement.ts: syncAllEnhancementTranslations() batches the
  whole catalog into one Lara call per locale (it's a handful of rows,
  not a large catalog like experiences — no need for the on-demand
  per-proposal targeting used there), skipping rows whose hash already
  has an "ok" translation.
- getEnhancements(locale) now merges in the translated row the same way
  getFullExperiences() does for experiences, via the existing
  getLocalizedExperience() helper (reused as-is, it's generic).
- Wired into /api/translate-proposal-experiences: runs alongside the
  experience translations on every proposal generation. Since the
  catalog rarely changes, this costs one real Lara call the first time
  and is then a no-op (hash match) on every subsequent proposal, so no
  separate backfill script or admin-save hook was needed for this.

